	(text "Cable (straight-through, both ends T568):\n  1, 2  +5 V from the master        7, 8  GND\n  3 / 6 master to head  (+ / -)     5 / 4 head to master (+ / -)\nSupply and ground each use both wires of one pair, so a wrong plug into\nan Ethernet port puts no voltage across a transformer winding.\n\nLooking at the meter with the cable leaving to the right, the meter's LED\nis on the right and its optical button on the left of the port centre:\nQ1 sits at +3.25 mm, D2 at -3.25 mm (IEC 62056-21, 6.5 mm apart)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20 262 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.5 1.5)
			)
